From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:27:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 177/179] feat(gastown): ship the polecat workspace-setup
 fences as a pack executable (gcp-xeael)

workspace-setup was about 270 lines of shell the model retypes every time it sets up a bead, and it is the second most common polecat restart point. The base-resolve, key-load/roots, artifact-worktree validator, worktree create/adopt and new-branch fences now live in gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-workspace.sh, and the step carries three 8-line stubs that locate the script and source it.

The script is SOURCED, not executed, so the cd into the task worktree, BASE_REF, WORKTREE and the validator functions land in the caller's shell exactly as the inline fences did. Run directly it prints WORKSPACE_USAGE and exits 2. Every formula substitution became an explicit positional argument, so the script holds no template text. Behaviour is identical: a throwaway identity harness diffed old and new over 91 paths under bash 5.3 and 3.2 with no differences (harness not committed).

Tests that extracted or pinned the moved text are re-pointed to the script (test_polecat_artifact_dir.sh, test_polecat_base_resolution.sh, the inference gate and its test), plus a new foreign-repo canonical-path case and test_polecat_workspace.sh for the behavioural cases. Applied verbatim from the seat-verified artifact in gcp-2qq67 (sha256 9390e833).

Validation: see the acceptance evidence recorded on gcp-xeael.
